WEBVTT

00:00:28.397 --> 00:00:30.703
That was titled "Essence."
I wrote it about my mom.

00:00:30.747 --> 00:00:33.184
This next piece
is also about my mom.

00:00:33.228 --> 00:00:35.186
-Uh, excuse me...
-Wrap it up, nerd.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.275
-I'm still...
-All right, I don't know
what this is called,

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:38.407
and I don't care.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.495
Two, three, four!

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.890
That's kind of loud!

00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:52.160
What is the meaning
of this intense bass?

00:00:52.203 --> 00:00:53.944
Are you mocking me?!

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.598
-I don't hear it on our side.

00:00:55.641 --> 00:00:57.165
It must be your equipment.

00:00:57.208 --> 00:00:59.384
Engineer K'noch, today you die!

00:01:00.472 --> 00:01:02.822
Will someone shut that up?!

00:01:06.478 --> 00:01:08.437
- You're welcome.

00:01:10.482 --> 00:01:12.049
Okay, whatever that was.

00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:14.138
Ladies and gentlemen,
"Requiem for a Hug."

00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:16.706
Captain says you're too loud!

00:01:16.749 --> 00:01:19.274
Oh, God, oh, no, no,
I'm so sorry.

00:02:30.258 --> 00:02:33.391
RANSOM:
First officer's log,
stardate 57501.4.

00:02:33.435 --> 00:02:35.959
TheCerritos is en route
to Cardassia Prime

00:02:36.002 --> 00:02:37.961
for the most amazing reason.

00:02:38.004 --> 00:02:40.920
Captain Freeman is going to be instrumental in brokering peace

00:02:40.964 --> 00:02:42.922
-between the... Uh, wait.

00:02:42.966 --> 00:02:44.924
Just... reading
a little message here.

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.535
Yada yada yada. Oh.

00:02:46.578 --> 00:02:48.580
Oh, no.

00:02:48.624 --> 00:02:52.018
The captain is not
gonna be happy about this.

00:02:52.062 --> 00:02:54.760
What the hell
are you talking about!

00:02:54.804 --> 00:02:56.284
I'm sorry, Captain Freeman,

00:02:56.327 --> 00:02:58.024
but we're moving the peace
negotiations to Vulcan.

00:02:58.068 --> 00:02:59.809
Nobody wants to go
to Cardassia Prime.

00:02:59.852 --> 00:03:02.203
The Cardassians
are creeping everyone out.

00:03:02.246 --> 00:03:05.554
But I already prepared a speech,I learned how to do the dance...

00:03:05.597 --> 00:03:07.120
I'm sure you'll be involved

00:03:07.164 --> 00:03:09.079
in the nexthistoric,
once-in-a-lifetime summit.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.124
For now, you'll be heading
to Gelrak 5

00:03:11.168 --> 00:03:14.127
and, uh, endowing them
with diplomatic trinkets.

00:03:14.171 --> 00:03:15.781
We're delivering gifts?

00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:16.782
Godspeed, Captain.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.265
I spent weeks learning how tobark out Cardassian small talk.

00:03:21.309 --> 00:03:23.311
Seems like they
just changed locations.

00:03:23.354 --> 00:03:25.530
-I don't think it was a slight
on the Cerritos.
-Yeah, right.

00:03:25.574 --> 00:03:27.663
Nobody respects us, because
we don't demand their respect.

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:29.230
This ship is a joke.

00:03:29.273 --> 00:03:31.710
Well, then we're the funniest
joke in all of Starfleet.

00:03:31.754 --> 00:03:33.538
Shut up, Jack!
I'm sick of it.

00:03:33.582 --> 00:03:35.192
We have to do something to prove

00:03:35.236 --> 00:03:37.194
that this crew isn't
a bunch of slackers.

00:03:38.935 --> 00:03:41.590
Okay, try it now.

00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:43.505
-Field strength is at..

00:03:43.548 --> 00:03:44.941
-Ooh!
-100%

00:03:44.984 --> 00:03:46.638
You almost phasered me!

00:03:46.682 --> 00:03:47.944
Calm down. It's set to...

00:03:47.987 --> 00:03:49.859
Uh, it was...
it was set to stun.

00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:51.817
Hey, Boimler, how's the field
integrity looking in there?

00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:54.124
Uh... oh!

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.518
It's good.

00:03:56.561 --> 00:03:58.955
Okay. Computer, margaritas.
Frozen. Salt.

00:03:58.998 --> 00:04:00.173
TENDI:
Wait, don't we have to report

00:04:00.217 --> 00:04:02.001
that we're done
so we can get a new task?

00:04:02.045 --> 00:04:04.352
Don't sweat it, baby girl-- likemany things, commanders have

00:04:04.395 --> 00:04:07.137
no idea how long it takes
to balance a phase variance.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.878
You never admit the actual
amount of time it takes

00:04:08.921 --> 00:04:11.097
to finish a job-- if you did,
your days would be packed.

00:04:11.141 --> 00:04:13.970
-Isn't that lying?
-No. It's creative estimating.

00:04:14.013 --> 00:04:15.406
When you get an assignment,

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.234
you exaggerate
how long it's gonna take,

00:04:17.278 --> 00:04:18.931
then you're a hero
when it's done early.

00:04:18.975 --> 00:04:20.977
Eh, it's just a little
buffer time. No biggie.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.370
And you're okay with this?

00:04:22.413 --> 00:04:24.763
No! If it were up to me,
we'd never take a break.

00:04:24.807 --> 00:04:26.504
But it's Lower Decks tradition.

00:04:26.548 --> 00:04:29.377
Tendi, how long will it take
to repair a biobed?

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.770
Oh, uh, that would take
about five...

00:04:31.814 --> 00:04:33.337
hours.

00:04:33.381 --> 00:04:34.556
Excuse me?

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:36.297
That's great!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.820
Aw, Tendi, look at us.

00:04:37.863 --> 00:04:39.648
Lower Decks--
breaching protocol together.

00:04:39.691 --> 00:04:41.302
Friendship!

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:48.352
Oh, be sure to stroll throughthe ship as slowly as possible.

00:04:48.396 --> 00:04:49.962
It's not like
we're busy exploring

00:04:50.006 --> 00:04:51.355
the mysteries of the cosmos!

00:04:55.359 --> 00:04:57.492
Does no one do any work
around here?!

00:04:57.535 --> 00:05:00.146
-Geez, there goes buffer time.
-What was that, Ensign?

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.800
Uh, nothing, Captain.

00:05:07.502 --> 00:05:08.807
-Uh...
-Bridge.

00:05:08.851 --> 00:05:10.418
Cap'n. I mean, Captain.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.725
Anything to report, Ensign?

00:05:13.769 --> 00:05:16.032
Uh, keeping busy.
I inventoried Cargo Bay Four,

00:05:16.075 --> 00:05:17.642
assisted with the baryon sweep

00:05:17.686 --> 00:05:20.036
of the warp nacelles,
skipped buffer time

00:05:20.079 --> 00:05:22.386
-and went straight to work on...-Turbolift halt!

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.823
What is "buffer time"?

00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:26.216
Uh...

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:31.264
What's up with you?
You're looking more, like,

00:05:31.308 --> 00:05:33.658
-weaselly than usual.
-Well, th-that's
just how my face looks.

00:05:33.702 --> 00:05:35.312
-You-you know that.

00:05:35.356 --> 00:05:36.792
WOMAN:
Oh.

00:05:36.835 --> 00:05:38.794
"Effective immediately,the Lower Deck scheduling deceit

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:40.404
will no longer be tolerated"?

00:05:40.448 --> 00:05:41.623
What scheduling deceit?

00:05:41.666 --> 00:05:43.407
Wait. Let me see.
"All assignments

00:05:43.451 --> 00:05:45.627
"must be completed and logged
in exactly the time mandated

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.369
-by command"?
-Are we being timed?

00:05:48.412 --> 00:05:49.935
"Failure to meet quotas
will not be tolerated."

00:05:49.979 --> 00:05:51.676
Ah, this is bad, this is bad.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.113
I-I thought it was tradition.I thought you said nobody cared.

00:05:54.157 --> 00:05:56.028
They didn't. There was no way
the captain noticed

00:05:56.072 --> 00:05:57.247
we were padding stuff out.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.379
Somebody ratted.

00:05:58.422 --> 00:06:00.598
I bet it was Delta shift.

00:06:00.642 --> 00:06:01.991
Yeah. Delta shift is the worst.

00:06:02.034 --> 00:06:03.601
They thinkthey're so much better than us,

00:06:03.645 --> 00:06:05.386
just becausethey're so much better than us.

00:06:05.429 --> 00:06:07.997
It doesn't matter who ratted.
We don't need buffer time.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.042
We're Starfleet.
We're the best of the best,

00:06:10.086 --> 00:06:11.957
and we can still get
everything done early.

00:06:12.001 --> 00:06:13.916
Boimler's right.
We don't need a buffer time.

00:06:13.959 --> 00:06:16.440
-We've got this!
-Yeah, no, yeah,
you're probably right.

00:06:16.484 --> 00:06:18.442
What's one less margarita a day?

00:06:30.541 --> 00:06:31.760
Excuse me!

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.720
Watch it.

00:06:35.764 --> 00:06:37.200
BILLUPS: Rutherford,
I need that diagnostic

00:06:37.243 --> 00:06:38.636
on the guidance system, now!

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.203
But now is right now!

00:06:40.246 --> 00:06:41.422
Move!

00:06:41.465 --> 00:06:43.032
-Move, move, move, move!
-Aah!

00:06:43.075 --> 00:06:44.642
Come on,
watch where you're going.

00:06:44.686 --> 00:06:46.644
Now I only have ten minutes
to do a 30-minute calibration.

00:06:46.688 --> 00:06:48.690
Stop yelling!

00:06:48.733 --> 00:06:49.995
Uh, sorry, wish I could help.

00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:51.649
I'm late for Ransom's
stupid away mission.

00:06:51.693 --> 00:06:53.521
T'ANA : Ensign
Tendi! You were supposed to be

00:06:53.564 --> 00:06:55.087
in sickbay 20 minutes ago!

00:06:55.131 --> 00:06:57.002
-I'm coming!
-Personal Log:

00:06:57.046 --> 00:06:59.091
I've completed all of today's
assignments ahead of schedule,

00:06:59.135 --> 00:07:00.615
and have requested more.

00:07:00.658 --> 00:07:03.139
-Space: The funnestfrontier?

00:07:04.619 --> 00:07:06.969
Ooh. Somebody's got to purge
the calibration matrix.

00:07:07.012 --> 00:07:08.274
I call dibs!

00:07:08.318 --> 00:07:10.363
BOIMLER:
♪ Ooh, I love purgin'

00:07:10.407 --> 00:07:12.670
-♪ I purge you, I purge you,
I purge you, I purge you ♪

00:07:12.714 --> 00:07:14.716
♪ I purge, purge, purge, purge,purge, purge, purge ♪

00:07:14.759 --> 00:07:17.283
♪ And a puh and an urge
and a puh and an urge ♪

00:07:17.327 --> 00:07:19.460
♪ Ooh, I love purgin'!

00:07:19.503 --> 00:07:21.766
All right, let's see
a little hustle there, guys.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.508
An away mission is only routineuntil it isn't.

00:07:24.552 --> 00:07:26.554
Horned gorillas, sentient tar,

00:07:26.597 --> 00:07:28.556
spores that make you hook upwith your best friend's sister--

00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:30.427
all disasters
I've personally experienced

00:07:30.471 --> 00:07:32.603
on missions that should
have been a walk in the park.

00:07:32.647 --> 00:07:34.213
Mariner, you're late.

00:07:34.257 --> 00:07:35.998
Uh, no, I've been here
the whole time, you know,

00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:38.914
loading stuff, hearing aboutgorillas, uh, spores, et cetera,

00:07:38.957 --> 00:07:41.046
that weird story you told usabout your best friend's sister.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:42.265
Get it together, Mariner.

00:07:42.308 --> 00:07:43.571
The captain has us
on a strict timetable.

00:07:43.614 --> 00:07:45.007
Well, then maybe you could help

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:46.748
instead of whatever you're doingright now.

00:07:46.791 --> 00:07:48.532
I am helping.
I'm commanding.

00:07:48.576 --> 00:07:50.534
You're lucky your
phaser accuracy is so high,

00:07:50.578 --> 00:07:52.710
or I'd never let you
beam off this ship.

00:07:52.754 --> 00:07:54.843
We wouldn't even be going
on a mission if the admiral

00:07:54.886 --> 00:07:57.585
hadn't downgraded the captain
to delivering gifts.

00:07:57.628 --> 00:07:59.978
-Come on, let's bail.
-No. And roll down
those sleeves.

00:08:00.022 --> 00:08:01.502
This isn't a barn.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:07.856
RANSOM:
The Gelrakians base
their entire social structure

00:08:07.899 --> 00:08:09.640
around crystals.

00:08:09.684 --> 00:08:12.338
When we land, we must display
the honor crystal they gave

00:08:12.382 --> 00:08:14.863
to the first contact team
to show that we come in peace.

00:08:14.906 --> 00:08:16.386
I should've tried that
with my ex.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:17.822
Yeah.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.913
I'm picking up an increase
in atmospheric hydromounds.

00:08:21.957 --> 00:08:23.262
Yeah,
they're called clouds, man.

00:08:23.306 --> 00:08:24.916
Just to be safe,
I'll disengage autopilot

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.483
and land her manually.

00:08:26.527 --> 00:08:28.050
That's literally
what the autopilot's for.

00:08:28.093 --> 00:08:29.747
It's a automatic pilot.

00:08:37.973 --> 00:08:39.322
-Perfect landing, sir.

00:08:39.365 --> 00:08:41.193
Not even my best work,
to be honest.

00:08:41.237 --> 00:08:43.587
-We could've just beamed down.
-I didn't catch that, Mariner.

00:08:43.631 --> 00:08:45.763
Uh, yeah I just said we should
get going, clock is ticking.

00:08:45.807 --> 00:08:47.373
Uh, productivity and et cetera.

00:08:47.417 --> 00:08:49.419
We'll go when I give the order.

00:08:50.551 --> 00:08:53.379
-Let's roll.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.301
Greetings. It is an honor to--

00:09:02.345 --> 00:09:05.087
Ensign Vendome,the honor crystal.

00:09:07.655 --> 00:09:10.309
-This isn't crystals.
-He's got wood. He's got wood!

00:09:10.353 --> 00:09:11.659
Uh-oh, that doesn't
sound peaceful.

00:09:11.702 --> 00:09:13.008
-Uh, uh...
-Where's the crystal, Vendome?

00:09:13.051 --> 00:09:14.618
Sir, I loaded the wrong case.

00:09:14.662 --> 00:09:16.881
This is a fertility totem
meant for Mavok Prime.

00:09:16.925 --> 00:09:18.448
I-I was rushing
to finish my tasks.

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:20.145
You dare insult us

00:09:20.189 --> 00:09:23.975
with this perverted woodensex charm of our sworn enemies?

00:09:24.019 --> 00:09:25.411
This is an act of war.

00:09:25.455 --> 00:09:27.631
Starfleet scum!

00:09:27.675 --> 00:09:29.981
-Vendome!

00:09:37.728 --> 00:09:39.687
There's too many of them.
Fall back!

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.384
Come on.

00:09:45.214 --> 00:09:47.172
-Oh, God, I'm gonna die!
-We live on a spaceship.

00:09:47.216 --> 00:09:49.522
-Nobody is dying
from a spear wound.

00:09:50.611 --> 00:09:51.916
Crystals!

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.136
-Oh. Hate when this happens.
-Oh!

00:09:54.179 --> 00:09:56.138
Let's just stun them
and get out of here!

00:09:56.181 --> 00:09:58.575
Negative, we just signed them
into the Federation.

00:09:58.619 --> 00:10:00.533
What this calls for
is some classic

00:10:00.577 --> 00:10:02.274
Jack Ransom peace brokering.

00:10:02.318 --> 00:10:03.449
Are you out of your mind?

00:10:03.493 --> 00:10:04.625
Watch and learn.

00:10:04.668 --> 00:10:05.974
This is gonna be awesome.

00:10:06.017 --> 00:10:08.367
Attention, Gelrakians,
I am Commander Jack--

00:10:08.411 --> 00:10:10.326
Ooh!

00:10:10.369 --> 00:10:12.502
All right, that wasawesome.

00:10:12.545 --> 00:10:14.809
-Ah, circled by spears.

00:10:14.852 --> 00:10:17.159
This is a classic.
What am I, Kirk?

00:10:17.202 --> 00:10:18.943
Is this the 2260s?
All right.

00:10:24.253 --> 00:10:27.169
Whoa, oh, hey, hey!

00:10:27.212 --> 00:10:28.692
Uh, we got acid here.

00:10:28.736 --> 00:10:30.781
Excuse me!

00:10:30.825 --> 00:10:33.784
Rutherford.

00:10:33.828 --> 00:10:35.220
Aah, Tendi, what the hell?

00:10:35.264 --> 00:10:36.352
Can't talk, got to work.

00:10:36.395 --> 00:10:37.396
I'm compiling.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.920
What?

00:10:38.963 --> 00:10:41.313
The impulse manifold needs
to be degaussed again.

00:10:41.357 --> 00:10:43.185
I have to assist with a surgery,

00:10:43.228 --> 00:10:45.883
and I honestly can't remember
which deck sickbay is on!

00:10:45.927 --> 00:10:47.711
-Uh, 26?
-Is that--?

00:10:47.755 --> 00:10:49.495
Do we have that many?

00:10:49.539 --> 00:10:50.975
COMPUTER:
Enter security code.

00:10:51.019 --> 00:10:53.456
-I'm waiting, Ensign.
-Sorry, Captain.

00:10:53.499 --> 00:10:54.892
Something's wrong
with the console.

00:10:54.936 --> 00:10:57.286
Move! I'll do it myself.

00:10:57.329 --> 00:10:59.810
Lieutenant Shaxs,
any word from the away team?

00:10:59.854 --> 00:11:03.422
Captain, the sensors have
picked up Gelrakian ships

00:11:03.466 --> 00:11:05.120
approaching
off the starboard bow.

00:11:05.163 --> 00:11:06.121
What?

00:11:06.164 --> 00:11:07.339
On screen.

00:11:07.383 --> 00:11:08.950
Are we supposed to be hosting

00:11:08.993 --> 00:11:10.255
a welcome dinner or something?

00:11:10.299 --> 00:11:12.170
Captain,
they're locking phasers.

00:11:12.214 --> 00:11:13.476
Really?

00:11:13.519 --> 00:11:14.651
Raise shields.

00:11:15.957 --> 00:11:17.872
-Shaxs?
-I'm trying, Captain.

00:11:17.915 --> 00:11:19.656
Something's wrong
with the controls.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.614
Ah, stupid controls.

00:11:21.658 --> 00:11:24.356
Do I have to run
this whole ship myself?

00:11:25.749 --> 00:11:26.750
SHAXS:They've launched boarding pods!

00:11:26.794 --> 00:11:27.795
Red alert!

00:11:31.189 --> 00:11:34.410
Repel all intruders,
but do not use it as an excuse

00:11:34.453 --> 00:11:35.933
to stop doing
what you are doing.

00:11:35.977 --> 00:11:37.587
I want to stay on track
and on time.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.589
It's called
multi-tasking, people.

00:11:39.632 --> 00:11:41.852
They do it on the Enterprise
all the time.

00:11:41.896 --> 00:11:44.028
I don't want to hear anycomplaining, I only want to hear

00:11:44.072 --> 00:11:46.161
repelling of intruders andpeople getting their work done!

00:11:48.772 --> 00:11:51.340
Swords and spears--how did these guys get on board?

00:11:55.083 --> 00:11:57.433
MARINER:
Hey, guy.

00:11:57.476 --> 00:11:59.435
Hey, guy?

00:11:59.478 --> 00:12:01.306
Hey, guy, is this whatyou wanted to do with your life?

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.526
Just capture people-- is thatwhat you dreamt of when you were

00:12:03.569 --> 00:12:05.789
a little whatever-you-are?
Are you fulfilled by that?

00:12:05.833 --> 00:12:07.791
-Yes.
-Wow, all right, uh...

00:12:07.835 --> 00:12:09.837
well, do you know what,
that means you're lame.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.926
-You're a loser.
-Hey, keep it down!

00:12:11.969 --> 00:12:14.363
I'm writing a speech that will
convince them to let us go.

00:12:14.406 --> 00:12:17.409
A speech, seriously?
Permission to speak freely.

00:12:17.453 --> 00:12:18.759
You always speak freely.

00:12:18.802 --> 00:12:20.325
Nobody can stop you
from speaking freely.

00:12:20.369 --> 00:12:21.631
All right, you know
what you've got going on?

00:12:21.674 --> 00:12:23.633
You have broad shoulders
and shiny hair

00:12:23.676 --> 00:12:25.853
and you talk a good game,
but when it comes to actually

00:12:25.896 --> 00:12:28.116
doing the job-- the job--
you don't have it.

00:12:28.159 --> 00:12:31.119
I'm calling bull
on your whole thing here, sir.

00:12:31.162 --> 00:12:33.469
You're so busy breaking protocolthat you never look ahead.

00:12:33.512 --> 00:12:35.471
One of these days you're going
to get someone killed, Ensign.

00:12:35.514 --> 00:12:36.994
With all due respect, sir,

00:12:37.038 --> 00:12:38.735
my friends aren't trapped
in an alien prison,

00:12:38.779 --> 00:12:40.302
your team is.

00:12:40.345 --> 00:12:42.695
That's not myteam,
it's ourteam.

00:12:42.739 --> 00:12:44.785
But I guess
you don't think that way.

00:12:44.828 --> 00:12:46.830
Here we go, show time.

00:12:46.874 --> 00:12:49.441
We may come
from different worlds,

00:12:49.485 --> 00:12:52.618
-but on the inside we are all---GERNBA: Silence, Starfleet!

00:12:52.662 --> 00:12:55.883
You are being held responsiblefor the lies of the Federation.

00:12:55.926 --> 00:12:58.059
Your trial will be by combat.

00:12:58.102 --> 00:12:59.887
Yes, now we're talking!

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.802
And by "talking," of course,
I mean "fighting."

00:13:01.845 --> 00:13:05.196
One of you must face
our greatest champion, Vindor.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:08.460
Usually we start the battle andVindor steps out of the shadows

00:13:08.504 --> 00:13:10.506
and it's super intimidating,
but he's here,

00:13:10.549 --> 00:13:13.552
so I'm just gonna show him
to you right now.

00:13:13.596 --> 00:13:15.641
Vindor.

00:13:15.685 --> 00:13:17.643
If you win, we let you go.

00:13:17.687 --> 00:13:20.995
If you lose, you'll be dead
and your away team

00:13:21.038 --> 00:13:24.041
will be crushed
by the adjudication geode.

00:13:24.085 --> 00:13:26.000
Crystals!

00:13:28.045 --> 00:13:30.613
Okay, I'm looking at
a lot of blank faces here.

00:13:30.656 --> 00:13:32.920
An adjudication geode is
a special type

00:13:32.963 --> 00:13:35.444
of constitutional crystal we useto legally smoosh our criminals.

00:13:35.487 --> 00:13:37.011
Here is your battle blade.

00:13:37.054 --> 00:13:39.665
You have one hour to choose

00:13:39.709 --> 00:13:42.190
who gets the honorof being slaughtered by Vindor.

00:13:42.233 --> 00:13:44.279
If you can't decide, we will--

00:13:44.322 --> 00:13:45.410
-I'll do it!
-I'll do it! Give it to me!

00:13:45.454 --> 00:13:46.498
-Yo, I touched it first.
-Give it, come--

00:13:46.542 --> 00:13:47.804
-Tell him! No, me!
-No, mine!

00:13:47.848 --> 00:13:49.023
You do realize you're
fighting over who gets

00:13:49.066 --> 00:13:49.937
to be chopped in half
by Vindor, right?

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:51.199
-Me, dibs!
-No, I said me,

00:13:51.242 --> 00:13:52.243
-I touched it first.
-Come on. Give it to me.

00:13:52.287 --> 00:13:53.505
-Jack Ransom-- it's mine!
-No! No!

00:14:01.078 --> 00:14:03.167
Aah!

00:14:03.211 --> 00:14:06.388
Translation--
"Bark hugging root smoochers"?

00:14:06.431 --> 00:14:08.999
What the heck
got these guys so wound up?

00:14:09.043 --> 00:14:11.436
Gah, this is totally gonna
mess up my schedule.

00:14:13.264 --> 00:14:14.657
-Don't move, human!

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:15.745
We have you surrounded.

00:14:15.788 --> 00:14:17.660
Yeah, but I-I have a phaser.

00:14:19.575 --> 00:14:21.185
These guys are lightweights.

00:14:21.229 --> 00:14:23.709
This is what
the red alert's about?

00:14:23.753 --> 00:14:27.148
Captain, I just phasered
some Gelrakians?

00:14:29.454 --> 00:14:32.022
-Um, hello?
-Intruder!

00:14:33.676 --> 00:14:35.765
Oh, it's just that huffy ensign.

00:14:35.808 --> 00:14:37.158
-Sorry, Brimler.
-I'm not huffy.

00:14:37.201 --> 00:14:38.550
Why aren't you at your post?

00:14:38.594 --> 00:14:39.682
We wouldn't even be
in this situation

00:14:39.725 --> 00:14:41.292
if you weren't slacking off.

00:14:41.336 --> 00:14:42.424
I'm not!

00:14:42.467 --> 00:14:45.253
Damn it!
We're 15 minutes behind.

00:14:45.296 --> 00:14:47.429
Our entire schedule is going
to be off for the month.

00:14:47.472 --> 00:14:49.431
Wait a minute-- clocks,

00:14:49.474 --> 00:14:51.694
time, schedules.

00:14:51.737 --> 00:14:54.566
You guys are under
the strict scheduling, too?

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:56.873
I have to be-- I'm manning
every station on my own.

00:14:56.917 --> 00:14:58.440
What? No, no, no, no, no.

00:14:58.483 --> 00:15:00.007
This is all wrong--
you're the captain!

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:03.010
I need us working harder
and faster and stricter!

00:15:03.053 --> 00:15:05.055
-GELRAKIAN: Where are you
hiding your crystals?!

00:15:05.099 --> 00:15:06.665
We don't have any crystals!

00:15:06.709 --> 00:15:08.972
I mean we do have dilithium,but we're not giving you those.

00:15:12.628 --> 00:15:15.152
Trial by combat is
my responsibility.

00:15:15.196 --> 00:15:17.807
I'm ranking officer, I'll be
fighting Vindor, end of story!

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:19.417
Rank means nothing right now.

00:15:19.461 --> 00:15:21.289
Rank means everything always!

00:15:21.332 --> 00:15:23.160
You know what, I doget off
on breaking protocol.

00:15:23.204 --> 00:15:25.510
I'm good at exploring
strange new worlds,

00:15:25.554 --> 00:15:27.991
solving space mysteries
and kicking asses.

00:15:28.035 --> 00:15:30.298
Protocol is for people that
need to be told what to do,

00:15:30.341 --> 00:15:32.343
which Idon't.
See this bad boy?

00:15:32.387 --> 00:15:33.692
Tentacle guy, bunch of arms.

00:15:33.736 --> 00:15:35.346
Stabbed me
with a barnacle blade.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.784
Check it out-- Magus III,
Nanibia Prime, Scottsdale.

00:15:38.828 --> 00:15:40.003
That was a mess.

00:15:40.047 --> 00:15:42.571
I earned every one
in high-concept fights

00:15:42.614 --> 00:15:43.702
just like this one.

00:15:43.746 --> 00:15:45.139
So? What do you got?

00:15:45.182 --> 00:15:47.228
-Let me see your scars.
-You know I don't have any.

00:15:47.271 --> 00:15:48.838
Because you play it safe.

00:15:48.881 --> 00:15:51.232
You said it-- that's ourteam
under that geode.

00:15:51.275 --> 00:15:54.061
Let me do what I'm good at,
let me save them.

00:15:54.104 --> 00:15:57.020
Sometimes you have to do
what's wrong to survive.

00:15:57.064 --> 00:15:58.500
You're right.

00:16:00.589 --> 00:16:03.244
What the ?!
Ah, God, oh!

00:16:03.287 --> 00:16:05.768
You stabbed me in the foot
with a battle blade!

00:16:05.811 --> 00:16:08.162
I'd rather die than let you
put your life on the line.

00:16:08.205 --> 00:16:09.554
Oh, you are such a psycho!

00:16:09.598 --> 00:16:10.642
What are you doing?

00:16:10.686 --> 00:16:12.209
Ow! Why?

00:16:12.253 --> 00:16:14.211
I'm the first officer
of a Federation starship,

00:16:14.255 --> 00:16:15.691
and your commander.

00:16:15.734 --> 00:16:18.085
And nobody crushes my team.

00:16:18.128 --> 00:16:19.651
Let's do this!

00:16:19.695 --> 00:16:22.350
CROWD :
Vindor! Vindor!

00:16:22.393 --> 00:16:24.091
Vindor! Vindor!

00:16:24.134 --> 00:16:25.788
Vindor!

00:16:29.009 --> 00:16:30.836
-Vindor?
-Come on, big guy.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.014
I only need my hands
for this one.

00:16:42.457 --> 00:16:43.893
Ha-ha-ha! Yah!

00:16:45.895 --> 00:16:47.984
-Ha-ha!

00:16:48.028 --> 00:16:49.812
-Double-fist punch!
-Oh!

00:16:53.076 --> 00:16:55.209
Whoa, that was actually
kind of hot.

00:16:55.252 --> 00:16:57.167
Ugh! Get it together, Mariner,
get it together.

00:16:57.211 --> 00:16:59.039
You are notinto this.
Come on.

00:17:07.569 --> 00:17:09.397
Let's see how much
those Federation wood lovers

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.964
like our crystal graffiti.
Ha-ha-ha!

00:17:15.446 --> 00:17:17.187
I-I need to get back to comms.

00:17:17.231 --> 00:17:18.971
-Captain, listen to me...
-Don't touch me!

00:17:19.015 --> 00:17:21.496
This is all my fault, thinking
I belong at a peace summit

00:17:21.539 --> 00:17:23.280
when I can't even keep
my own ship together.

00:17:23.324 --> 00:17:24.760
What? Captain, no.
You did nothing wrong.

00:17:24.803 --> 00:17:26.240
Your schedules, your rules--

00:17:26.283 --> 00:17:28.024
this has been
the greatest week of my life.

00:17:28.068 --> 00:17:29.330
You run the tightest ship
in Starfleet.

00:17:29.373 --> 00:17:30.940
Captain, we need to act now!

00:17:30.983 --> 00:17:33.116
"Tightest ship."
Then why is it falling apart?

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:34.770
Because not everyone is
a Boimler.

00:17:34.813 --> 00:17:36.772
This crew has their limits.
They're only human.

00:17:36.815 --> 00:17:38.469
Well, and Vulcan.
And Orion.

00:17:38.513 --> 00:17:40.123
There's that Benzite guy
in Tactical...

00:17:40.167 --> 00:17:41.994
Damn it, man!
If you're trying to inspire

00:17:42.038 --> 00:17:44.171
some sort of resolution,
then inspire it now!

00:17:44.214 --> 00:17:46.651
Ugh, it kills me to say this,
but for the good of the ship

00:17:46.695 --> 00:17:48.305
we have to... loosen up.

00:17:48.349 --> 00:17:50.525
Loosen up? But then we're
right back to buffer time.

00:17:50.568 --> 00:17:52.396
Yes, when people could do
whatever they had to

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:53.789
to get the job done.

00:17:53.832 --> 00:17:57.227
You're a great captain.
Let them be a great crew.

00:17:57.271 --> 00:17:58.663
You're... you're right!

00:17:58.707 --> 00:18:00.709
I ama great captain!

00:18:03.146 --> 00:18:05.105
Attention all decks:
as of now,

00:18:05.148 --> 00:18:08.456
I am authorizing
all crew to break any rule,

00:18:08.499 --> 00:18:11.850
abandon any protocol,
and cut any corner to defend

00:18:11.894 --> 00:18:13.287
theCerritos.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.897
You are Starfleet--

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:18.248
Do what you have to do
to take back this ship.

00:18:18.292 --> 00:18:19.293
Buffer time!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.958
-RANSOM: I demand

00:18:33.002 --> 00:18:34.525
a peaceful negotiation. Yah!

00:18:34.569 --> 00:18:36.614
-I respect your sovereignty.

00:18:36.658 --> 00:18:38.790
Mm, so ethical.

00:18:46.015 --> 00:18:47.147
Interlocked hands!

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:48.583
Stop! Stop! I submit!

00:18:48.626 --> 00:18:50.628
I thought
you only said "Vindor."

00:18:50.672 --> 00:18:52.848
It's so the other guys think
I'm strong and dumb.

00:18:52.891 --> 00:18:55.024
But I'm not.
I love to read!

00:18:55.067 --> 00:18:58.549
Well, all right,
you're free, you're all free.

00:18:58.593 --> 00:19:00.508
Everybody's free.

00:19:02.597 --> 00:19:04.729
-Whoo-whoo! Starfleet!

00:19:04.773 --> 00:19:07.079
Oh, I see how it is--
you're gonna stab me, but then

00:19:07.123 --> 00:19:08.951
you don't stab Vindor? What
are your priorities, Ransom?

00:19:08.994 --> 00:19:10.257
I ju... Whoa!

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.128
We got to stop doing
trial by combat,

00:19:12.172 --> 00:19:14.217
or we'll never get to use
the geode.

00:19:14.261 --> 00:19:16.567
How about a regular trial,
with a judge?

00:19:16.611 --> 00:19:18.221
And instead of the geode...

00:19:18.265 --> 00:19:19.962
-Oh! We could do a death race!

00:19:20.005 --> 00:19:22.051
Start building a crystal car!

00:19:23.313 --> 00:19:24.619
Crystals.

00:19:28.623 --> 00:19:30.277
Ha-ha!

00:19:32.931 --> 00:19:34.194
-Ooh!

00:19:37.197 --> 00:19:39.242
Oh!

00:20:02.526 --> 00:20:05.486
Hey, sorry about the whole
"invading your ship" thing.

00:20:05.529 --> 00:20:07.923
You know?
Very un-crystal-like of us.

00:20:07.966 --> 00:20:10.099
Don't worry about it.
I'd rather be here with you

00:20:10.142 --> 00:20:12.319
than with those freaks
on Mavok Prime.

00:20:12.362 --> 00:20:14.321
Wood-worshiping freaks, right?

00:20:14.364 --> 00:20:16.279
-Come on.

00:20:16.323 --> 00:20:18.890
T'ANA :
You'll be fine.

00:20:18.934 --> 00:20:20.936
Want me to clean up
those disgusting scars?

00:20:20.979 --> 00:20:23.286
Uh, no way.
No. These are my trophies.

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.289
Congratulations, you look like
a  scratching post.

00:20:26.333 --> 00:20:27.943
-Mariner.
-Commander.

00:20:27.986 --> 00:20:29.814
I would appreciate it
if you give me a heads-up

00:20:29.858 --> 00:20:32.077
before you file your report.It would give me some extra time

00:20:32.121 --> 00:20:34.210
to pack up my free weights--
there's a ton of 'em.

00:20:34.254 --> 00:20:36.560
-What report?
-For stabbing you
with a battle blade.

00:20:36.604 --> 00:20:38.214
That's a guaranteed
court-martial.

00:20:38.258 --> 00:20:40.303
I am not filing a report,
actually.

00:20:40.347 --> 00:20:42.349
But... I thought you hated me.

00:20:42.392 --> 00:20:44.089
You talk about yourself
a little too much,

00:20:44.133 --> 00:20:45.743
but stabbing me,
breaking protocol--

00:20:45.787 --> 00:20:47.484
that was actually pretty cool.

00:20:47.528 --> 00:20:49.747
Sometimes I forget
what Starfleet's all about,

00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:51.967
and today you reminded me.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:54.317
Plus, this is gonna make
a good scar.

00:20:55.492 --> 00:20:57.277
A great scar.

00:20:58.713 --> 00:21:01.150
-Take her away, boys!
-W-Wait, what? Why?

00:21:01.193 --> 00:21:02.760
Because you ignored me
when I ordered you

00:21:02.804 --> 00:21:04.762
to roll down your sleeves.
They're against code.

00:21:04.806 --> 00:21:07.069
The sleeve thing?
You're an idiot.

00:21:07.112 --> 00:21:09.898
You just earned an extra day
in the brig!

00:21:09.941 --> 00:21:12.074
Joke's on you, man--
I love the brig!

00:21:12.117 --> 00:21:14.685
I'm going to my favorite place!

00:21:14.729 --> 00:21:18.036
Next time, I'm gonnalet somebody kill you.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:20.082
I'm gonna dance in your blood!

00:21:20.125 --> 00:21:23.433
Okay. That was kind of hot.

00:21:24.521 --> 00:21:26.480
-Come.

00:21:26.523 --> 00:21:29.047
-You wanted to see me, Captain?-It took the eyes of a child

00:21:29.091 --> 00:21:31.528
to see whatwe were blind to today, Boimler.

00:21:31.572 --> 00:21:33.661
If it wasn't for you,
we would still be following

00:21:33.704 --> 00:21:35.271
every little rule in the book.

00:21:35.315 --> 00:21:36.664
Wait, is that bad?
'Cause I loverules.

00:21:36.707 --> 00:21:38.448
We're instituting
a new ship-wide mandate,

00:21:38.492 --> 00:21:41.059
and we're calling it
the "Boimler Effect."

00:21:41.103 --> 00:21:42.757
Really? I-I'm honored.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.541
You should be.
The Boimler Effect is about

00:21:44.585 --> 00:21:46.369
encouraging shortcuts
and preventing people

00:21:46.413 --> 00:21:48.328
from just blindly following
the rules.

00:21:48.371 --> 00:21:50.460
From now on, the crew
can build in buffer time

00:21:50.504 --> 00:21:51.766
whenever they deem fit.

00:21:51.809 --> 00:21:53.463
Congratulations. Dismissed.

00:21:53.507 --> 00:21:55.813
Oh. Well, hey,how about we add a little thing

00:21:55.857 --> 00:21:58.033
about how important it is
to blindly followrules?

00:21:58.076 --> 00:22:00.296
If my name is going
to be associated with...

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:02.690
No, the Boimler Effect isliterally the opposite of that.

00:22:02.733 --> 00:22:05.388
But I don't know, I don't know
how I feel about that, and...

00:22:05.432 --> 00:22:07.999
I-Is it in ink? Is it already
in the system? Is it...

00:22:08.043 --> 00:22:09.784
BOIMLER:
Wow, it's on a plaque.

00:22:09.827 --> 00:22:12.569
Get back to your stationand do whatever
youdeem right.

00:22:14.615 --> 00:22:17.269
BOIMLER:
I get a whole rule
named after me,

00:22:17.313 --> 00:22:19.359
and it's all about
notfollowing rules.

00:22:19.402 --> 00:22:20.969
Don't worry about it, man.

00:22:21.012 --> 00:22:23.406
They're always making upnew rules no one ever remembers.

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:25.277
I'm sure this one
will fade, too.

00:22:25.321 --> 00:22:26.888
Yeah, this isn't something
to worry about.

00:22:26.931 --> 00:22:28.368
No one will remember.

00:22:29.673 --> 00:22:31.675
PROFESSOR:
Which is why

00:22:31.719 --> 00:22:34.939
the Boimler Effect issomething we will never forget.

00:22:34.983 --> 00:22:36.637
So named after the laziest,

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:39.509
most corner-cutting officer
in Starfleet history,

00:22:39.553 --> 00:22:41.381
Brad Boimler,

00:22:41.424 --> 00:22:44.688
seen here with one of
the great birds of the galaxy.

00:22:44.732 --> 00:22:47.648
Anyway, let's move onto somebody even more important,

00:22:47.691 --> 00:22:51.042
perhaps the most important
person in Starfleet history,

00:22:51.086 --> 00:22:53.915
Chief Miles O'Brien.

00:23:34.303 --> 00:23:37.306
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:24:23.483 --> 00:24:24.484
Chirp.
